  "_about": "Norway's 48 national parks, 41 on the mainland and 7 on Svalbard. IDs are permanent: user logs point at them. 'name' is the park's short official name (Miljødirektoratet's 'navn', first form); 'naturvernId' keys it to the Naturvernområder dataset, from which the pipeline reads the outline, official names in every language, municipalities and manager. Founding dates and areas are curated in each guide's facts with their source, since 'vernedato' is the current regulation's date. 'reachedBy' is how a park with no road to it is reached, in a line taken from its guide's directions; a trip shows it where no road route exists.",
